# Standalone: close and reopen after every plugin update

macOS does not hot-reload the Standalone `.app`. **Do not only remind the user** — when this rule applies, you **must** run the shell relaunch below so the new binary is actually loaded.

## When this rule applies

Apply at the **end of the same turn** if **any** of these happened:

- You edited files under `Source/` (engine, audio, UI, tests that compile into the plugin), or `CMakeLists.txt`, or other targets that change the SculptSampler binary, **or**
- You ran `cmake --build` (or equivalent) and the SculptSampler / Standalone build **succeeded**.

**Skip** this rule if the turn only changed docs, `.mdc` rules, images, or other files that do **not** require a rebuild to test audio.

## Mandatory action (agent)

From the **workspace root** of this repo, run **exactly** (one line; `killall` may exit 1 if the app was not running — that is OK):

```bash
killall SculptSampler 2>/dev/null; open "build/SculptSampler_artefacts/Debug/Standalone/SculptSampler.app"
```

- Use **Debug** path above unless this turn only built **Release** — then use `build/SculptSampler_artefacts/Release/Standalone/SculptSampler.app` instead.
- After running it, **state in your reply** that Standalone was quit (if running) and reopened from that path.

## Why `killall`

`open` alone can focus an **already-running** old process. **`killall SculptSampler` first** guarantees the next `open` starts a fresh instance with the new build. Unsaved plugin state in Standalone may be lost — that is acceptable for dev iteration; if the user only uses AU/VST in a host, say so once and remind them to rescan/reload that format separately.

## Summary line

In the same turn as a qualifying change, your user-visible summary should include **both**: (1) what changed, and (2) that Standalone was relaunched via the command above.
